    {
      "id": "note-overview",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": -460,
        "y": 0
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "Three splits from one CSV: 20% test, then 25% of the rest as validation, both stratified so every species keeps its share. Then the check most pipelines skip: does any evaluation row also appear in training? Iris has a repeated row, and the top row finds 0 of 30 validation rows and 1 of 30 test rows also appear in the training split. Removing exact repeats before splitting (150 rows, 1 exact repeat removed, 149 left) brings it to 0 of 30 validation rows and 0 of 30 test rows also appear in the training split. A leaked row is scored from memory, so it makes validation and test accuracy look better than they are.\n\n從一個 CSV 切出三份：先切 20% 當測試資料，剩下的再切 25% 當驗證資料，兩次都分層抽樣，讓每個品種維持原本的比例。接著是多數流程會跳過的檢查：評估用的列有沒有也出現在訓練資料裡？iris 有一列重複，上面那一排找到 驗證資料 30 列中有 0 列、測試資料 30 列中有 1 列也出現在訓練資料裡。切分之前先移除完全重複的列（150 列，移除 1 列完全重複，剩下 149 列），結果變成 驗證資料 30 列中有 0 列、測試資料 30 列中有 0 列也出現在訓練資料裡。外洩的列靠記憶就能答對，會讓驗證與測試正確率看起來比實際好。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "start",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": -460,
          "y": 0
        },
        "noteWidth": 400
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-groups",
      "type": "note",
      "position": {
        "x": 2097,
        "y": 1061
      },
      "data": {
        "noteKind": "text",
        "noteContent": "Exact repeats are the easy case. Near repeats leak too: several photos of the same object, or several rows from the same patient. Split by that group (object, patient, user) rather than by row.\n\n完全重複是簡單的情況。幾乎重複的也會外洩：同一個物體的好幾張照片、同一位病人的好幾筆資料。這時要依群組（物體、病人、使用者）切分，而不是逐列切分。",
        "noteColor": "#3d3d1a",
        "boundToNodeId": "leak-after",
        "boundOffset": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 437
        },
        "noteWidth": 320
      }
    }
